okay so we've been talking more and more  about Donald Trump's impeachment and  calls for impeachment and I want to step  back from that for a moment and just  talk about sort of some historical  parallels between Richard Nixon in 1974  and Donald Trump in 2019 and the top  level parallels are pretty obvious right  at the top level we have a attempt to  obstruct investigations into their  respective presidencies cover-up  attempts and this is the kind of  broadest way in which Nixon 74 and Trump  20 19 or similar but as Kelby Adams  points out in a really good multi post  thread on Twitter articles of  impeachment against Nixon were filed in  part for using his power as president  directly and through subordinates to  impede obstruct an investigation into  the Watergate Hotel break-in the second  part of the Nixon impeachment articles  was for violating the constitutional  rights of citizens or contravening the  laws governing agencies of the executive  branch when you look at the Moller  report it literally spells out examples  of Trump doing the same thing all over  the place if you look at pages 77 and  113 of the first volume of the report if  you look at pages 177 and 178 of Part  two pay special attention to footnote 10  91 about impeachment not substituting  criminal liability in the Moller report  which maybe we'll talk about tomorrow we  learn that Donald Trump prevented aides  from testifying before Congress another  example of obstruction and there are a  whole bunch of other examples we could  go through which already gives us  parallels for two out of three of the  impeachment articles filed against  Richard Nixon that we can find in the  Trump administration then we get to the  third part of Nixon's articles of  impeachment quote failing without lawful  cause or excuse to produce papers and  things as directed by duly authorized  subpoenas issued by the Committee on the  Judiciary of the House of  Representatives this is part three of  Nixon  impeachment articles and it exploded  over the weekend for Donald Trump we  found out that Trump has been directing  his entire administration to simply not  provide documents not respond to  subpoenas not show up and testify when  it comes to some individuals in the  Justice Department and this is above and  beyond the tax returns okay which aren't  even really a part of this Donald Trump  and everyone around him have tried to  use their power to obstruct the full  investigation into a whole bunch of  different stuff including the Trump  Tower meeting including financial crimes  on and on and on so there are a lot of  similarities if you look at the articles  of impeachment of Richard Nixon but then  let's go even further Trump and Nixon  both hated and regularly attacked the  media Trump's framing is if not for the  press unfairly targeting me none of this  impeachment talk would even been going  on nothing would even have been going on  none of the Moller probe or a lot of the  Moller probe would never have gotten  going if it weren't for the evil press  Nixon had almost the same position Nixon  thought that the media made him lose to  John F Kennedy in 1960 he would  regularly ramble against the media etc  etc and very very similar attacks when  you look at presidential power Nixon at  his core didn't care about the limits of  presidential power Trump similarly dozen  obstructing investigations installing  puppet cabinet members firing people and  trying to fire even more people one of  those that he failed to get fired was  Robert Muller himself  when Don McGann said I'm not going to do  it both Nixon and Trump lost top-level  staff to scandals and criminality that  was part of the bigger picture of what  was going on in the Nixon administration  and there's a long list of people that  both Trump and Nixon lost I won't name  them all former elected Republican  officials some Republicans are now  running for office who are saying it's  time for Trump to go but ultimately what  saves Trump is a key difference between  1974 and 2019  in 2070 for eventually it became known  to Nixon that elected Republicans were  turning on him elected Republicans  recognized they are not going to be able  to continue their support for President  Nixon and it is going to have to be a  yes vote on conviction on impeachment  and that is ultimately what caused  Richard Nixon to resign I don't know  that you're going to see that with  Donald Trump in 2019 because Republicans  in 1974 were willing to go beyond  partisanship and they realized Nixon  horribly damaged the country and he  needs to be removed so far we have not  seen that same point of view from any  prominent current elected Republicans  we've seen it from some former  Republicans we've seen it from george w  bush's former speechwriter we see it  from william weld who's running a  primary campaign against donald trump  but you need two-thirds of the senate to  convict on impeachment democrats can't  do it now democrats can't even do it if  they do well in 2020 in the senate  because you need a two-thirds majority  which democrats are not going to have  after the 2020 election  so unless 2019 becomes like 1974 and  that republicans realize this is this is  just bad for the country we have to  cross party lines here you are not going  to see impeachment of the President of  the United States  one other note on this impeachment of  Nixon actually failed before it  succeeded in getting him to resign  before the Watergate break-in in 72 some  Democrats already believed that it was  time to impeach Nixon you had House  resolutions 975 976 and 989 they were  all submitted to the House Judiciary  and they went nowhere in 72 in 73 there  was an attempt to impeach Nixon for  something unrelated to the Watergate  break-in for Nixon's secret bombing of  Cambodia articles of impeachment were  introduced by congressman Robert Dryden  at the time and that didn't go anywhere  so understand that these are very long  processes and at this point in time  aside from my opinion as to whether  Trump should be impeached I genuinely  would not be a  to say whether the evidence suggests  impeachment is or is not likely because  if history tells us anything these  things can be extraordinarily  unpredictable and have a very very long  time period during which they develop we  will see the similarities between Nixon  74 and Trump 2019 growing by the day if  you love learning new things you  probably want to check this out the  david pakman show today is sponsored by  Skillshare and we're giving you two  entire months of free access to  Skillshare when you click the link  underneath this video Skillshare is a  vibrant online learning community  offering more than 25,000 video classes  on just about anything you can think of  get better at playing an instrument  learn to use Photoshop how to edit  videos they have classes on drawing  painting business cooking nutrition  personal productivity and I'm not even  really scratching the surface I recently  took a great class on introductory  watercolour painting I'm still not good  but I am learning and you can access the  entire library of fun easy-to-use online  courses for free for two months by using  the link underneath this video two  months of learning something that's  totally new to you something you want to  get better at something you already love  or you can get ahead in your career by  learning new skills that will help you  at your job I've gotten a ton out of it  Pat has taken some courses that he's  found really valuable and I think you'll  love it to get started for free by  clicking the link under this video
 

